+	Let $A$ and $B$ be finite nonempty sets and let $e\colon A \to B$. If every fiber $e^{-1}(b)$ has the same cardinality $c$, then the push-forward of the uniform distribution on $A$ along $e$ is the uniform distribution on $B$.
